  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe release site tests (`python -m unittest discover -s site/tests -v`) failed on v0.25.0 and on `main`. This PR makes the guide content match the shipped app. It changes a test only where the test was wrong.\n\nContent (site/):\n- Copy six app icons from `assets/ui/` to `site/static/icons/` (byte-identical): `op-slot-undercut`, `op-v-carve`, `tool-t-slot`, `tool-keyseat`, `tool-dovetail`, `tool-lollipop`. `op-v-carve` is new on `main` since v0.25.0.\n- Copy `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` to `site/static/icons/LICENSES.txt`. The notice did not have the Agie processor section. The icon failures hid this failure.\n- `operation-paths.svg`: add the `SlotUndercut` and `VCarve` views.\n- `operations-2d.md`: add the Slot Undercut picture. Add a V-Carve section (icon, picture, tool, picks, settings, refusals). The values come from `vcarve_op.rs` and `vcarve_page.rs`. The catalog block of the new heading is the same as the `cargo xtask catalog` output.\n- `operations/_index.md`: list V-Carve in the Milling 2D row.\n- `post-processors.md`: add the `rotariesBeforeTraverse` row (from 56e81ffc8 and `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`).\n- `first-4axis-part.md` and `tools.md`: the label is now **Tool number** (`tool_settings_grid.rs`), not \"Tool number (0 = next free)\" or \"Tool number (0 = list position)\".\n\nTests (site/tests/):\n- Cause 1: `section_lead` skips one leading, well-formed generated catalog block. Then the icon must be the first content of the section. A missing icon, a block lower in the section or an unclosed block still fails. The reason is in `docs/decisions/3271-site-test-drift.md`: xtask owns the block under the heading, and its `--check` holds it there. The generator does not change.\n- Cause 3: `FAMILIES` lists `SlotUndercut` and `VCarve` (both are in `OpType` now).\n- Cause 5: 028495f5c gave the AI chat pane its transport, so \"no live transport endpoint\" is not true now. The check names the limits that the guide states and that still hold: \"no key entry form\" and \"no endpoint field\".\n- Cause 6: `test_continuous_a_claims_match_the_shipped_machine` does not read `docs/decisions/` now. The cut moves those files into `RECOMMENDED.md`. The shipped A axis travel stays checked from the saved machine in the project test.\n- Cause 7: the label checks read `tool_settings_grid.rs` and `op_page/header.rs`, where the labels are drawn now. The \"Tool number\" label follows the UI.\n\nNo UI or Rust change is in this PR.\n\n## Readings\n\n`ZOLA=<zola 0.23.6> PYTHONUTF8=1 python -m unittest discover -s site/tests`:\n- before (`main` dfbe0d8a5): 82 tests, 76 failures, 1 error.\n- after: 82 tests, OK.\n\n`cargo xtask catalog --check`: pass (12 cases checked; the page links are as the generator writes them).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The `release.yml` site job on Linux. The local run used Windows with the pinned zola 0.23.6 (Windows build).\n- On Windows without `PYTHONUTF8=1`, the navigation tests fail with `UnicodeDecodeError` (cp1252 `read_text()`). This is not new and CI runs on Linux; this PR does not change it.\n- `tools.md` still says \"Zero means the tool's position in the document tool list\". The UI hint says \"leave at 0 to assign the next unused number\". This PR changes only the label; the meaning needs a check against the code.\n\nChangelog: none\nProcess change: no\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3271\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
